From 22f0d153b4d96551a90c942870d5ed817d5e0d82 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Kenan Sulayman <kenan@int.mov>
Date: Tue, 20 Oct 2026 04:51:21 +0200
Subject: [PATCH] feat(core): add execution and memory budget tracking across
 cobra-core

Introduce `cobra/core/Budget.h` with thread-local execution contexts (`budget::Context`, `budget::Scope`), memory accounting (`budget::Ledger`, `budget::Allocator`), and periodic `budget::Checkpoint()` checks for deadlines, cancellation callbacks, and allocation limits.

- Replace standard containers across `cobra-core` with budget-aware aliases (`BudgetVector`, `BudgetMap`, `BudgetSet`, `BudgetFlatMap`).
- Override `Expr::operator new` and `Expr::operator delete` to account for AST node allocations via `budget::AllocateObject` and `budget::FreeObject`.
- Insert `budget::Checkpoint()` calls across hot loops, recursive traversals, and non-Tracy `COBRA_ZONE` macros, and guard grid size calculations with `budget::CheckedProduct`.
- Update `lib/core/CMakeLists.txt` to support subproject builds by using relative include paths and guarding `find_package` calls when `absl` or `hwy` targets are already defined.
